From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mrmikedrum <mrmikedrum@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 19:26:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Make game copies match the game they copy

GameCopier left out much of a game in progress, so a copy resumed from a
priority stop could play differently from the original. On 4-player
Commander games, a copy taken at each AI priority matched the original
(every zone in order, permanents' state, the stack and its targets,
priority) about 76-87% of the time, and 0.6-3.8% of copies failed.

- The stack: triggered and activated abilities are copied too, not only
  spells, with their triggering objects, targets, X and chosen modes; a
  variant the card doesn't list is copied from the ability itself. Cast
  and targeting triggers are suppressed while the stack is built.
- The turn: who has priority and had it first, the phase counters, and
  the spells cast this turn and last turn.
- Dungeons keep their piece type and room; effect cards (player
  keywords, the monarch) are copied whole; Radiation's effect card is
  not made twice.
- Commanders, effect cards and remembered cards are also found by id,
  as a card that changed zones is a new object with the same id.
- Players who have left the game are out of the copy, and combat drops
  defenders the copy doesn't have.

On the same probe afterwards: 5596 of 5600 copies match, none fail.
-Dforge.copier.trace=true reports stack entries left out of a copy.

Goldfish-Upstream: offer

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
